      "goal": "Describe states and say where people and things are.",
      "note": "**Estar** is for temporary states, as in Castellano: **Estic cansat.**\n\nFor *where* something is, Catalan traditionally uses **ser**: **On és el lavabo?** **Soc a casa.** Estar is also heard and accepted, but ser is the more genuine choice.\n\nWatch the preposition: *en casa* → **a casa**, *en Madrid* → **a Madrid**.",
      "tables": [
        {
          "title": "estar — present",
          "rows": [["jo", "estic"], ["tu", "estàs"], ["ell, ella, vostè", "està"], ["nosaltres", "estem"], ["vosaltres", "esteu"], ["ells, elles, vostès", "estan"]]
        }
      ],
      "vocab": [["cansat", "cansado"], ["content", "contento"], ["tancat / obert", "cerrado / abierto"], ["enfadat", "enfadado"], ["el lavabo", "el baño"], ["la botiga", "la tienda"]],
      "items": [
